  "median-of-two-sorted-arrays": {
    "trick": "Binary search how many elements the smaller array contributes to the left half (i), so the larger array contributes half − i. The partition is right when both left sides ≤ both right sides, and the median comes from the four values at the border.",
    "steps": [
      "Make A the shorter array. half = (m + n + 1) // 2.",
      "Binary search i in [0, m], with j = half − i. Missing borders count as ±∞.",
      "If A[i−1] > B[j], move left. If B[j−1] > A[i], move right.",
      "Odd total → max of the left borders. Even → average of max(left borders) and min(right borders)."
    ],
    "time": "O(log min(m, n))",
    "space": "O(1)",
    "pitfall": "Searching over the longer array, or forgetting the ±∞ sentinels at the edges.",
    "code": "class Solution:\n    def findMedianSortedArrays(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int]) -> float:\n        A, B = (nums1, nums2) if len(nums1) <= len(nums2) else (nums2, nums1)\n        m, n = len(A), len(B)\n        half = (m + n + 1) // 2\n        lo, hi = 0, m\n        while lo <= hi:\n            i = (lo + hi) // 2\n            j = half - i\n            a_left = A[i - 1] if i > 0 else float(\"-inf\")\n            a_right = A[i] if i < m else float(\"inf\")\n            b_left = B[j - 1] if j > 0 else float(\"-inf\")\n            b_right = B[j] if j < n else float(\"inf\")\n            if a_left <= b_right and b_left <= a_right:\n                if (m + n) % 2:\n                    return float(max(a_left, b_left))\n                return (max(a_left, b_left) + min(a_right, b_right)) / 2\n            if a_left > b_right:\n                hi = i - 1\n            else:\n                lo = i + 1"
  },
